Methods & Pipeline Description
Quality control and host read filtering : Raw sequencing reads are preprocessed using Trimmomatic [1] to remove adapter sequences and filter out low-quality bases. Cleaned reads are aligned against the human reference genome (GRCh38) using STAR [2]. Unmapped reads (non-human fraction) are retained and extracted for downstream microbial profiling.

Taxonomic profiling and minimizers extraction : Taxonomic classification is performed on the unmapped reads using Kraken2 [3] with a confidence score threshold of 0.2 against the PlusPFP reference database. To ensure robust taxonomic assignment on low-biomass samples, minimizer statistics (total minimizers and unique minimizers per taxon) are extracted using the --report-minimizer-data flag and consolidated across samples.

ROC-calibrated systematic decontamination : To eliminate batch effects, kitome contaminants, and false-positive algorithmic assignments, an empirical decontamination filter is implemented using receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve analysis (pROC package [4]). The optimal threshold is determined via Youden's J statistic [5], combining cross-cohort ubiquity/prevalence across non-digestive control tissues and unique minimizer coverage calibrated on digestive positive reference controls. Taxa identified above the contamination threshold are compiled into an exclusion blacklist.


